# (build 105) The CRT page's HDR row and its own page: HDR, PEAK and WHITE
# (docs/crt.md). A 3840x2400 panel fullscreen whose SDL says HDR with a
# headroom of 6.25 over an SDR white of 2.5 (x 80 nits): PEAK's AUTO is
# 6.25 x 2.5 x 80 = 1250 nits. Left and right step PEAK through its stops
# (AUTO, 400 ... 10000) and WHITE by 10 nits to 400, 50 above; C on HDR's
# row of the CRT page opens the HDR page, B comes back. Without HDR, AUTO
# is 1000 and HDR says NO HDR. The route reads its own settings.json.
start new
wait screen title
display 3840x2400 fullscreen hdr=6.25/2.5
press esc
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press up
expect crt hdr OFF
press right
expect crt hdr ON
press c
expect crt hdr ON
expect crt peak AUTO 1250 NITS
expect crt white 200 NITS
wait ticks 6
shot hdr_page_auto
press down
press right
expect crt peak 400 NITS
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
expect crt peak 1000 NITS
press left
press left
press left
press left
press left
press left
expect crt peak AUTO 1250 NITS
press left
expect crt peak AUTO 1250 NITS
press c
expect crt peak 400 NITS
press down
press right
expect crt white 210 NITS
press left
press left
press left
expect crt white 180 NITS
wait ticks 4
shot hdr_page_white_180
press c
expect crt white 190 NITS
# The screen goes SDR: AUTO falls back to 1000, HDR says why.
display 3840x2400 fullscreen
expect crt hdr ON / NO HDR
expect crt peak 400 NITS
press up
press left
press left
expect crt peak AUTO 1000 NITS
wait ticks 6
shot hdr_page_no_hdr
press b
expect crt hdr ON / NO HDR
press b
expect escape-menu open
press b
expect escape-menu closed
